          "code": "RULE:DES-006",
          "severity": "warning",
          "path": null,
          "message": "Interference between units is possible. Randomize at a level that contains the interaction (clusters of players), or set population.interference to none_expected and record why."
        },
        {
          "code": "RULE:DES-008",
          "severity": "warning",
          "path": null,
          "message": "No pre-period covariate declared. Declare design.pre_period_covariate: the name of a column of the experiment's outcomes file that holds, for each player, a measure taken before the player's first exposure, for example the primary metric over the week before. The results review then shows the adjusted estimate, which is the registered analysis, beside the unadjusted one, and checks that the covariate is balanced across the arms. A measure taken after the treatment can act would remove part of the real effect."
        },
        {
          "code": "RULE:HYP-002",
          "severity": "warning",
          "path": null,
          "message": "Primary metric has no governed reference. Define the metric in docs/metrics/ and set primary_metric.governed_reference to that file."
        },
        {
          "code": "RULE:PRO-003",
          "severity": "warning",
          "path": null,
          "message": "No guardrail metrics declared. Declare at least one guardrail with its harmful direction and a tolerance, for example a refund rate that must not rise by more than 10% relative."
        },
        {
          "code": "RULE:DES-009",
          "severity": "info",
          "path": null,
          "message": "The cohort check of the results review would not run on this plan. If an effect that differs between the weeks players joined could matter for this change, plan at least 21 days (42 days or more allows blocks of 14 days, which need fewer players a week), bring in more eligible units each day or give the smaller arm a larger share, keep the arms within 9 to 1, and randomise and analyse in the same independent unit (player, user or device). The evidence gives the units a day that pass with even arrivals; allow more, because arrivals vary (design section 21.6: spiky arrivals need 1.5 to 3 times as much). Otherwise accept that the cohort check will not run: the other results checks are not affected."
        },
        {
          "code": "RULE:PRO-004",
          "severity": "info",
          "path": null,
          "message": "Bucketing salt not declared. Set procedure.bucketing_salt to a value unique to this experiment, for example its id."
        },
        {
          "code": "SIZE_DIFFERS",
          "severity": "warning",
          "path": "stated.required_total_players",
          "message": "the draft states 20000 players; Referee's power plan for these inputs needs 16,412 players. Referee's figure is the one reported"
        }
      ],
